    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0242" n="234" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg234"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/221</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-27">May 27, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Ambassador called at his request. He read a despatch from Anthony
                    Eden, Foreign Minister, in which he offered profuse apologies for the tone and
                    nature of a recent <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> regarding some
                    phases of the Pacific area which the British Ambassador, on his last visit to my
                        office,<anchor n="7" xml:id="d151-f1"/> proposed that I should receive and
                    file, but which he retained after some rather vigorous comment on my part. The
                    truth is that the Foreign Minister had all of his facts wrong.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
